{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug resolution — a453 symptom already remediated on origin/main (no new fix authored)\n\nResuming this in_progress bug. The decisive new fact the prior Phase-1 RCA did not yet have: **the red-gate symptom is already fixed on `origin/main`, and the gate is green again.**\n\n### The gate is GREEN\n- Scheduled run **33285210617** — sha `454f875e05d9`, 2026-08-30T01:14:19Z — **success**. (The three prior scheduled runs 33269532975 / 33253701193 / 33239620291 were red; this is the first green after the bridge landed.)\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor d0bcd6202789 454f875e05d9` → true; the green sha carries the raised budget (`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 563200`).\n\n### What fixed it (not me)\nCommit **`d0bcd6202789`** (`rebar-ticket: a8ba-a2a3-e9c8-4ffa` — task *\"W3 bridge: raise verify-identity pack budget to 550 MiB while 536b reclaim lands\"*, landed 2026-08-29 16:31, now **closed**) raised `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` from 102400 (100 MiB) to **563200 (550 MiB)** — ~70 MiB headroom over the ~481 MiB blobless tickets pack — with a self-documenting comment naming the restore ticket `fluorspar-comparable-zeren` (0894-b9b8-6590-4904). It also moved the one coupled test expectation (`test_pack_guard_contract`) in lockstep; the guard's fail-closed control flow is unchanged.\n\n### Why this satisfies a453's acceptance criteria\n- **AC1** (size-pack reproduced & attributed by object type/ref) — met by the Stage-1 dossier: 481 MiB observed / 464 MiB reproduced, **~90% Git tree objects** (428,022 trees ≈ 401 MiB), ~10% commits, **zero blobs** (filtered).\n- **AC2** (root cause of the 08-23 crossing: growth vs limit-too-low) — met: a **step-change** ~10× surge in `tickets` commits from 08-21 (≈120K commits — over half the branch — in 8 days), organic ticket-write activity fanned by the enrichment quartet + auto-reconcile merges, crossing a **static, unchanged** budget. Not a code regression; no workflow/limit/digest-schema change occurred near 08-23.\n- **AC3** (either the limit is intentionally re-set **with justification**, or growth reclaimed, **with evidence of a passing run**) — **met via the \"limit intentionally re-set\" branch**: a8ba's justified, reversible bridge + green run 33285210617.\n\nAC#3 is an explicit disjunction and the re-set-limit arm is satisfied, so a453 is resolved **by its own contract**.\n\n### Independent verification of the load-bearing RCA facts (I re-checked, did not just trust prior comments)\n- The guard measures the **tickets-inclusive** pack: `actions/checkout@v7` runs `filter: blob:none, fetch-depth: 0` (all refs → pulls the `tickets` orphan branch) and the `size-pack` guard runs **before** the separate \"Mount tickets branch\" step. Confirmed by reading `verify-identity.yml`.\n- The 100 MiB limit is a **deliberate canary**, not accidental: introducing commit `16a1a385` (ticket 037b, 2026-08-01) — *\"Add blobless fetches and executable pack-size budgets. Guard authorship verification with exact object-database snapshots so identity scans cannot lazily fetch promisor objects.\"*\n- No workflow/limit change caused the 08-23 crossing: `git log --since=2026-08-20 origin/main -- .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` shows only the **post-hoc** bridge `d0bcd6202789`.\n\n### Why no new code fix is warranted (and would be wrong)\nThe verifier is not broken and the blobless pack is not a compatibility bug — the guard is a growth canary that **fired correctly** on genuine store growth (independently corroborated by the data-disk-high alarm 5a05). The only levers are **policy/design changes**: (a) raise the budget — a *weakening of the growth canary*, already done as an explicit temporary bridge by a8ba; (b) reclaim historical Git objects — epic **536b** (causal-stability GC); then restore the budget to 100 MiB — task **0894**. Authoring another change here would be redundant with a8ba and would not shrink the pack. Per the debug protocol's not-a-bug/policy guard and the standing instruction to escalate authorship-verification policy changes, the budget-raise decision was correctly made *outside* this bug (a8ba, reviewed + landed), and the durable reclaim is owned by 536b/0894.\n\n### Attribution\n`caused_by → 4520-11a6-7458-454f` (apparent-sighted-cockatoo) already recorded (explicit). Chain: correctness fix `be8a0c0` deliberately removed enrichment-event pruning (correct in itself) and created an unbounded-retention obligation that 4520 was opened to bound but which remains unbuilt; the growth-management plan was incomplete. Scope-of-work omission, no single introducing commit → `plan_defect` escape.\n\n### Disposition\nClosing a453 as resolved: gate green, all ACs met via a8ba's landed bridge. The persisting underlying growth (bridge, not cure) is tracked by **536b** (reclaim) + **0894** (restore budget to 100 MiB). Linking a453 `relates_to` a8ba (resolving change) and 0894 (restore follow-up) for traceability."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788063921705928330,"uuid":"a71e1a8e-44bb-419d-a987-fdc736c03653"}